# .dockerignore for apps/abacus.
#
# NOTE: the production image builds with the railyard repo ROOT as context
# (see Dockerfile header), and that build already avoids target/ by copying
# only manifests + crates. This file additionally keeps the abacus subtree lean
# for any `docker build apps/abacus` (context = this dir) and for tooling that
# honors a subtree ignore file.

# Rust build artifacts (493MB+ locally — never ship into a build layer).
target/
**/target/

# Local runtime state written by the proxy (audit log, open-holds snapshot).
*.jsonl
abacus-open-holds.json
**/*.jsonl

# Operator-copied real config (secrets/identities). Only the *.example.json
# templates are tracked; never bake a live copy into an image.
config/*.json
!config/*.example.json

# Editor / OS / VCS noise.
.git
.gitignore
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~

# Docs and the Dockerfile itself do not belong in the build layer.
README.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
